<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed weaker at 0.67 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed weaker at 0.67 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.3070 to the dollar, down from 3.2945 on Tuesday and at 1.8780 to the mark, down from 1.8770, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 0.67 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, weaker than Tuesday's 0.89 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
